                "word": "pincher",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f239ee64-2c88-4543-becf-8f2a3c13bab9",
                        "entry_id": "a1a35f34-c7bd-33e8-b659-a6bea8af1e51",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pinchers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc15dbec-eb95-30d0-bed9-ad9b2c4d5614",
                        "entry_id": "a1a35f34-c7bd-33e8-b659-a6bea8af1e51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person or thing that pinches, as in squeezing; e.g. a miser or penny pincher."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c33cf453-d2a6-48ec-9cf7-03b6840a7f26",
                                "sense_id": "bc15dbec-eb95-30d0-bed9-ad9b2c4d5614",
                                "text": "The troubles can be endless: a mix-up on meals, a shortage of liquor, engine difficulties, other mechanical quirks, male pinchers, female whiners, vomiting children, two-timing stewardesses who steal your man, and, once in awhile,^([sic]) a plane that takes a good friend to a fiery death."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22f81c2d-44ae-39ce-8abf-20a451888d1a",
                        "entry_id": "a1a35f34-c7bd-33e8-b659-a6bea8af1e51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person or thing that pinches, as in stealing; e.g. a thief or kleptomaniac."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c104ef10-63af-4a71-b2b7-a6b118e0a7ad",
                                "sense_id": "22f81c2d-44ae-39ce-8abf-20a451888d1a",
                                "text": "“And they would certainly take offence, were their son to be accused of theft.” “It would stir them up like an egg whisk. I mean, however well they know that Wilbert is a pincher, they don't want to have it rubbed in.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8a0111b-f890-4e4e-837e-0cd637bb3a71",
                                "sense_id": "22f81c2d-44ae-39ce-8abf-20a451888d1a",
                                "text": "“And if ever a man needed to be constantly under an eye, it's the above kleptomaniac.” “The what?” “Haven't you been told? Wilbert's a pincher. […] He pinches things. Everything that isn't nailed down is grist to his mill.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "677ecc58-ead0-3105-97b2-cf1730925ccf",
                        "entry_id": "a1a35f34-c7bd-33e8-b659-a6bea8af1e51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dated form of pincer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "dated"
